==Hebrew==

===Etymology 1===
{{he-rootbox|ח־ת־ל}}
Of indeterminate origin, possibly a [[Wanderwort]]. First attested in the Hebrew of the {{w|Babylonian Talmud}}. Related to {{cog|tmr|חֲתוּלָא}}, a plural form of which appears in the {{w|Targum Jonathan}} version of Isaiah 13:22, rendering the Hebrew {{m|hbo|אִיִּים|t=jackals}} as {{m|tmr|חֲתוּלִין|t=cats}}. Compare also {{cog|ar|قط|4=|tr=qiṭṭ|id=cat}}, {{cog|la|cattus}}.

